{
  "about": [
    "The cases that fail TODAY, each with the audit finding(s) whose fix will make it pass (the port-parity audit of 2026-09-29; its plan is pact-gateway/docs/release/port-parity-2026-09-29.md).",
    "js/cases/known.mjs says how js/parity.mjs reads this: a case that fails exactly as `fails` says is excused; a case that fails otherwise, a case that passes with an entry here, and an entry for a case nobody has all fail the run; a port that threw is never excused. So this list can only shrink.",
    "The stage that fixes a finding deletes the entries its fix closes (the run names each one). The last stage deletes this file and its mechanism.",
    "`fails` is how the case fails, as js/parity.mjs names it: `differ` (the two ports answer differently), `<port> off the contract` (an answer contract/contract.json does not allow), `<port> not as expected` (an answer other than the one the spec or CONTRACT §0 fixes for it; a case that misses it is not compared besides).",
    "S1-<n> are divergences the generated cases found that the audit did not file; `new_findings` says what each is."
  ],
  "new_findings": {
    "S1-1": "open_result with no envelope (absent or null) answers `envelope_invalid` 'envelope members' in both ports, where CONTRACT §0 says an absent member is `bad_request` 'envelope is required'; open_result's note ('every refusal of the ENVELOPE is envelope_invalid') does not settle which. Reconcile the contract, then the ports.",
    "S1-2": "The contract contradicts itself, and both ports answer as its notes do: §0 says an absent member answers '<name> is required', while wallet_issue's note fixes 'vault_plaintext is required: the root lives there' and 'record_plaintext is required: the ledger lives there', and limits_decide's note fixes 'now is a time in milliseconds' for an absent `now`. Reconcile the contract; the ports follow.",
    "S1-3": "export_read_end reads an absent or null `lines` as 0 in both ports (and so answers the count refusal 'manifest.json: counts: messages is 3, and messages.jsonl holds 0 lines'): a zero value, where §0 says 'lines is required'."
  },
